|<center>[[Image:icon-bastion.png|75px|link=Bastion]]<br />[[Bastion]]</center>
|<small>Bastion's extremely high damage output in {{al|Configuration: Assault}} is more than capable of ripping you to shreds through your barrier, if you get caught in the open. Even if you manage to pin him with {{al|Charge}}, Bastion's high health, Armor and {{al|Ironclad}} passive allow him to survive the impact and often leave him healthy enough even to kill you right after. If Bastion is in Assault mode, get behind cover, and engage him when the ability ends.</small>
|<small>Guarding a friendly Bastion will be mutually beneficial; you'll be protecting him from oncoming fire, and he'll be able to mow down oncoming opponents. Just keep in mind that you are only able to guard what's in front of you; be wary of enemies trying to flank you from the rear. While you are able to walk off with ease, your Bastion will need a second to convert to Recon Configuration. While you should try to protect your Bastion, you also need to be in a mutual agreement of when you need to hold your ground and when you need to retreat, because if you run off and the Bastion didn't get the memo, he'll be torn apart, and you will be next.</small>
|-
|<center>[[Image:icon-cassidy.png|75px|link=Cassidy]]<br />[[Cassidy]]</center>
|<small>Cassidy can do a lot of damage to you with his {{al|Flashbang}} and Fan the Hammer when up close. When he uses {{al|Deadeye}}, put up your barrier to give your team time to get behind cover. Do not try to block it for an extended amount of time with your barrier, as the first bullet fired at your team will likely break your shield, making it unable to protect anyone else.</small>
|<small>Since both you and Cassidy love to take close-range engagements, this allows you to follow up on what he does and shield him when needed.</small> <small>In addition,</small> <small>Earthshatter and Deadeye</small> <small>can</small> <small>make a deadly combination:</small> <small>you set up the killshots, Cassidy pulls the trigger.</small>
|-
